;; The race (issue #17, clojure -M:race): one server per runner, these bots on it, each from a
;; landing cell of its own to the target. Sized by the capacity experiment (ci/capacity.edn, run
;; 38333898855, PR #35): a 4-core runner is CPU-bound, not memory-bound. The bots' JVM takes about
;; 9% of a core per bot and three cores from 30 bots up; the server's main thread takes the fourth
;; from 20 up, and past 30 its ticks run 60-90 ms. Memory never neared a limit (5 GB or more free
;; at 150 bots), so the heaps are generous: spare heap keeps collection rare on a CPU-bound box.
{:race/runners 20 ; GitHub runners
 :race/servers 1  ; servers per runner, each its own world copy, race process and bots
 :race/landing-sets ["R1" "R2" "R3" "R4"] ; ci/gym.edn's race worlds: runner r races on set (r-1) mod 4
 :race/bots 20             ; bots per server: the most before the four cores run out (400 racers in all)
 :race/prefix "Clj_r"      ; bot names: Clj_r01, Clj_r02, ...
 :race/until "nether"      ; the target; the run plays every step up to it (plan/through)
 :race/timeout-ms 19500000 ; 5 h 25 min, inside the runner's six hours
 :race/stagger-ms 3000     ; between bots joining: fresh players generating chunks at once time each other out
 :race/server-heap-mb 4096 ; the server's JVM: live about 0.8 GB + 0.06 GB a bot
 :race/bot-heap-mb 4096}   ; the one JVM all the bots share: live about 0.02 GB a bot
